-- The transverse-field Ising chain H = −Σ σz_i σz_{i+1} − g Σ σx_i, gapped for g ≠ 1 (gap 2|1 − g|) and critical at g = 1,
-- with e₀ known in closed form (Pfeuty 1970). A patch on k sites with bond weights b_i and field weights a_i (integers,
-- M = −Σ b_i σzσz − Σ a_i σx) is a valid local certificate when Σ a_i = g Σ b_i: translating it along the chain gives
-- (Σ b_i)·H, so e₀ ≥ λ_min(M)/Σ b_i. The weights at the patch's ends are free within that constraint (a gauge of the
-- certificate); Anderson's choice is half the field at each end. In the σx basis (true: σx = −1) the field is diagonal
-- and a bond flips two neighbours; all off-diagonal entries are ≤ 0, so the lowest state is positive: it lies in the
-- even sector and, for palindromic weights, in the mirror-symmetric one, and the patch is reduced to the orbits of the
-- even states under the mirror: G = BᵀMB, N = BᵀB over the orbit sums, a generalized problem for chem/inertiaq.cub.
lc-even : List Bool → Bool
lc-even s = case s of
  nil → true
  cons b r → if b then not (lc-even r) else lc-even r
